# AI Integration for Weather Insights

This plan outlines the integration of an AI service (Google Gemini) into the SkyCast web application to generate smart, natural language weather insights based on current weather data.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The backend requires a valid `GEMINI_API_KEY` to be added to the `.env` file for the AI integration to work. You will need to obtain an API key from Google AI Studio and place it in `backend/.env`.

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> Do you have a specific tone or style you want the AI to use? (e.g., formal, humorous, concise, travel-focused). The current prompt asks for a "helpful, concise, and friendly weather summary with clothing or activity recommendations." 

## Proposed Changes

### Backend Requirements

#### [MODIFY] backend/requirements.txt
Add `google-genai` to dependencies.

#### [MODIFY] backend/.env and backend/.env.example
Add a placeholder for `GEMINI_API_KEY`.

---

### Backend Implementation

#### [MODIFY] backend/main.py
- Import `google-genai` and initialize the client using the `GEMINI_API_KEY`.
- Create a new `Pydantic` model `WeatherInfo` to accept incoming weather data.
- Add a new `POST /api/weather/ai-insights` endpoint. This endpoint will:
  - Take the `WeatherInfo` payload.
  - Construct a prompt asking for a short summary and recommendation.
  - Call `client.models.generate_content` (using `gemini-2.5-flash`).
  - Return the AI's generated text as JSON.

---

### Frontend Implementation

#### [MODIFY] frontend/index.html
- Add an "AI Insights" section to the `main-content` area.
- Add an `id="ai-insight-text"` container and a loading state element specifically for the AI response.

#### [MODIFY] frontend/styles.css
- Style the AI Insights section using the existing `glass-card` classes.
- Add styles for the AI loading spinner to ensure it doesn't block the rest of the weather data rendering.

#### [MODIFY] frontend/app.js
- In `updateUI()`, after the main weather data has been loaded and displayed, asynchronously call `fetchAIInsights(state.currentData)`.
- Create the `fetchAIInsights` function to:
  - Show the AI loading state.
  - Make a `POST` request to `/api/weather/ai-insights` with the current weather.
  - Hide the loading state and display the AI-generated text.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run the FastAPI backend server using `uvicorn`.
- Trigger the `/api/weather/ai-insights` endpoint using a tool like curl or the Swagger UI (`/docs`).

### Manual Verification
- Start the frontend and search for a city.
- Ensure the main weather data loads immediately.
- Ensure the AI Insights section shows a loading spinner, then populates with a natural language summary and recommendation based on the weather conditions.
